      },
      "description": {
        "en": "Beihai is a prefecture-level city in the south of Guangxi, People's Republic of China. Its status as a seaport on the north shore of the Gulf of Tonkin has granted it historical importance as a port of international trade for Guangxi, Hunan, Hubei, Sichuan, Guizhou, and Yunnan.",
        "zh-CN": "北海市是中华人民共和国广西壮族自治区下辖的地级市，位于广西南部，北部湾沿岸。南流江由北向西南流入海。",
        "zh-TW": "北海市是中華人民共和國廣西壯族自治區下轄的地級市，位於廣西南部，北部灣沿岸。南流江由北向西南流入海。"
      },
